---
description: Integration documentation guidelines
globs: [
  "fe-tich-hop/*.md",
  "docs/**/integration/**/*.md",
  "docs/res/**/*.md"
]
alwaysApply: false
---
- Start docs with `# <Feature> Integration Guide`, a concise overview, and a “Source of Truth” list linking to backend router/service files.
- Add `## Authentication & Roles` describing required headers plus a permission matrix (`role → can read/write`).
- Under `## Use Cases`, create `### Use Case – <name>` sections containing Goal, Primary actors, Preconditions, and a Given/When/Then flow that references concrete endpoints (HTTP method + path).
- Each use case must embed at least one Draft API Sample (curl or fetch) plus request/response payloads that mirror the documented flow; label the snippet “Draft API Sample”.
- Include `## Endpoint Details` with a table (`Method | Path | Purpose | Module file`) and subsections listing params, filters, and response fields referencing real files (e.g. `packages/ai-edu-backend/modules/lesson/lesson.school-router.ts`).
- Finish with `## Type Definitions` that link to the source file path and inline the relevant `type`/`interface` blocks inside ```ts fences.
- Add `## Error Handling & Edge Cases` for behaviors that differ from defaults and `## Testing Notes` when QA steps or mocks are required.
- Keep bilingual vi/en wording only if the existing doc mixes both; otherwise default to concise English.
